      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel-Style Two-Number Calculator\n\nA tiny offline calculator with a chunky pixel look. Enter two numbers, pick an operation, and press **Calculate**.\n\n## Features\n\n- Two number inputs (`left`, `right`) that accept negative values and decimals\n- Operation selector: add, subtract, multiply, divide\n- Result appears without any label, just the number (or `Error`)\n- Rejects empty inputs, non-finite values, and division by zero with exact text `Error`\n- Keyboard accessible: all controls are labeled, and pressing Enter in either input calculates\n- Responsive layout that works from 360px wide\n- No packages, no network requests, no storage — just three files\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. Type a number in **Left** and another in **Right**.\n3. Choose an operation from the dropdown.\n4. Click **Calculate** or press Enter.\n\nThe result box shows only the numeric result, or `Error` when the input is invalid or you try to divide by zero.\n\n## Files\n\n- `index.html` — structure and required IDs\n- `styles.css` — pixel-themed styling and responsive layout\n- `script.js` — calculation logic and error handling\n\n## Notes\n\nEverything runs locally. There are no external assets, imports, or server requirements.",
